{title: It is good to give thanks}
{subtitle: Psalms 92:1–2}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb/D] | [Eb] | [Bb] [Bb/D] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A [Bb]psalm for the Sabbath [Eb]day
It is [Gm7]good to give [Bb/F]thanks to the [Eb]LORD
to sing [Gm7]praise to your name, [F]O Most High [Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
It is [Bb]good to give [Bbmaj7/D]thanks to the [Eb]LORD
[F]to sing [Gm7]praise to your [Bbmaj7/D]name, O Most [Eb]High
[F]to de[Gm7]clare your steadfast [F]love in the morn[Eb]ing
and your [Cm7]faithfulness [F]through the [Bb]nights [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
On the [Bb]ten-stringed lute and on [Bb/D]the [Eb]harp
to the [Gm7]melody of [Gm7/D]the [Eb]lyre
For [Gm7]you have made me [F]glad by your [Eb]work
O LORD, I [Gm7]sing for joy [F]at your [Eb]hands
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
It is good [Bb]to give thanks [Bb/D]to the [Eb]LORD
[F]to sing [Gm7]praise to your [Bb/D]name, O Most [Eb]High
[F]to de[Gm7]clare your steadfast [F]love in the morn[Eb]ing
and your [Cm7]faithfulness [F]through the [Bb]nights
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Your deeds of [F]hands bring me [Bb]joy
[Eb]Your work makes [F]my heart [Gm7]glad
O LORD, I [Eb]praise you [F]al[Gm7]ways
In morning [Eb]light and through the [Fsus4]night
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
It is [Bb]good to give [Bb/D]thanks to the [Eb]LORD
to sing [Gm7]praise to your [Bb/D]name, O Most [Eb]High
to de[Gm7]clare your steadfast [F]love in the morn[Eb]ing
and your [Cm7]faithfulness [F]through the [Bb]nights
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
It is good to give [Bb/D]thanks to the [Eb]LORD
[F7sus4]to sing [Gm7]praise to your [Bb/D]name, O Most [Eb]High
{end_of_verse}
